    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #157\n\n- 2026-09-11 19:59Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-11 20:54Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #384 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-157-generic-rest-08-09-expose-typed-querie-thr_fwdt7s22r8` to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #157: typed queries and relation mutations for the generic REST layer. - `POST /api/databases/:id/query` and `POST /api/views/:id/query` accept `{ filter, sort, cursor, limit, inTrash? }`, compile through the same shared typed filter/sort engine (`queryItemsCore` in `viewQuery.ts`), and return `{ items, nextCursor }`. Ad-hoc database queries and view queries over equivalent input produce identical results. - Deterministic keyset pagination via `id > cursor` under default order; limit defaults to 50 (upstream caps at 200); deleted rows excluded unless `inTrash: true`. - `PUT`/`DELETE /api/items/:id/relations/:propertyKey/:targetItemId` resolve `:propertyKey` to a property id and go solely through the existing audited relation choke-point (issue #82) — direction normalization, cardinality, paired properties, and ownership are enforced there, never re-implemented at the route layer. - Both routes always return the full authoritative envelope (item page or relation edge), never an empty 204. - Added `cardinality_violation` (409) to the closed error-code enum. - `deleteRelation`'s return type widened from `void` to `RelationEdge | null` so the DELETE route can return the deleted edge or a proper 404. Tests cover query parity between database/view routes, stable non-duplicating pagination, `inTrash` visibility, `validation_failed` for malformed filter/sort/limit/cursor/inTrash, and relation-route coverage for direction normalization, every cardinality, paired definitions, foreign/missing property keys, and owner violations. `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit/integration/e2e — 1298 tests) and `web/pnpm run verify` (139 tests) both pass. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 21:11Z — This issue was resolved by #384, which just merged into develop.",
